{"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/init(ratios:equivalenceRatio:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/equivalenceRatio","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/TuningSystem-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"JustIntonation","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/UsingIvorTuning"]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A just intonation system is defined by a set of frequency ratios relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tonic, each derived from small-integer harmonics. Any number of tones per interval of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equivalence is supported — from a simple pentatonic to Harry Partch’s 43-tone 11-limit scale.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On initialization, ratios outside ","type":"text"},{"code":"[1, equivalenceRatio)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are reduced by dividing by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"equivalenceRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" until they fall in range; exact multiples of ","type":"text"},{"code":"equivalenceRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(including 1:1) are silently discarded. The remaining ratios are deduplicated and sorted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios","type":"reference"},{"text":" property prepends the tonic (1:1) and appends the interval of equivalence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so it always spans one complete interval of equivalence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Does not support standard pitch notation. Just intonation systems are too variable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to map reliably to the 35 pitch classes of standard notation: even 5-limit scales","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contain enharmonic pairs that are distinct in just intonation but share a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spelling, and higher-limit systems diverge further or exceed the 35-pitch-class maximum.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/justintonation"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/EqualTemperament","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/LinearTemperament","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard"],"title":"Tuning systems","generated"